// Enable on @Configuration class:
@EnableMethodSecurity  // Spring Security 6 (was @EnableGlobalMethodSecurity before)
@Configuration
public class SecurityConfig { ... }

// Use on service methods:
@Service
public class UserService {

    @PreAuthorize("hasRole('ADMIN')")
    public void deleteUser(Long userId) { ... }

    @PreAuthorize("hasRole('USER') or #userId == authentication.principal.id")
    public User getUser(Long userId) { ... } // user can get their own data

    @PostAuthorize("returnObject.owner == authentication.name")
    public Document getDocument(Long docId) { ... } // check after loading
}
```

```java
// @Secured — simple, role-based only:
@Secured("ROLE_ADMIN")  // must include ROLE_ prefix!
public void adminAction() { ... }

@Secured({"ROLE_ADMIN", "ROLE_MANAGER"})  // OR logic
public void managerAction() { ... }

// @PreAuthorize — SpEL, flexible:
@PreAuthorize("hasRole('ADMIN')")
public void adminAction() { ... }

@PreAuthorize("hasRole('USER') or #userId == authentication.principal.id")
public User getUser(Long userId) { ... }

@PreAuthorize("isAuthenticated() and #email == authentication.name")
public void updateEmail(String email) { ... }
```

```java
// Role checks
@PreAuthorize("hasRole('ADMIN')")
@PreAuthorize("hasAnyRole('ADMIN', 'MANAGER')")
@PreAuthorize("hasAuthority('DELETE_USERS')")

// Authentication state
@PreAuthorize("isAuthenticated()")
@PreAuthorize("isAnonymous()")

// Method parameter access
@PreAuthorize("#userId == authentication.principal.id")
public User getUser(Long userId) { ... }

// Combining conditions
@PreAuthorize("hasRole('ADMIN') or #userId == authentication.principal.id")
public User getOrUpdate(Long userId) { ... }

// String comparison
@PreAuthorize("authentication.name == #email")
public void updateProfile(String email) { ... }
```

**URL-based** (SecurityFilterChain):
```java
.requestMatchers("/admin/**").hasRole("ADMIN")
// Anyone with ADMIN can access ANY /admin/** URL
// Coarse-grained — URL pattern only
```

**Method-level** (@PreAuthorize):
```java
@PreAuthorize("#userId == authentication.principal.id or hasRole('ADMIN')")
public User getUser(Long userId) { ... }
// Fine-grained — checks user owns data OR is ADMIN
// Works regardless of how the service is called
```

